      "username": "The_Justifier",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
      "created_at": "2023-02-24T00:56:21.112Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Semantics.  A scientist is allowed to make a prediction of what he thinks the outcome will be, as long as he never ignores data contrary to that preconception.  It’s human nature to anticipate, so the idea that you shouldn’t expect the most probable outcome is nonsense.  You simply shouldn’t be too surprised when it turns out differently from what you thought it would do.</p>",
